⚠️ UNCHECKED BLOCKS BYPASS SOLIDITY 0.8.0+ PROTECTION!

Solidity 0.8.0+ has automatic overflow/underflow checks,
but 'unchecked' blocks disable this protection.

❌ DANGEROUS if user input involved:
unchecked {
balance += amount;  // Can overflow!
total = a * b;      // Can overflow!
}

✅ SAFE usage (loop counters only):
for (uint256 i = 0; i < items.length;) {
// Process items[i]

unchecked {
++i;  // Safe: loop counter can't realistically overflow
}
}

✅ SAFE usage (guaranteed no overflow):
unchecked {
// Safe: subtraction after comparison
if (a >= b) {
result = a - b;  // No underflow possible
}
}

❌ NEVER use unchecked for:
- User-supplied values
- Token amounts
- Financial calculations
- Multiplication of arbitrary values

Only use unchecked when:
1. Loop counters (i++, ++i)
2. Mathematically proven safe
3. Gas optimization with careful review

Every role should have a clear admin hierarchy:

✅ DEFINE ROLE HIERARCHY:
bytes32 public constant DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE = 0x00;
bytes32 public constant MINTER_ROLE = keccak256("MINTER_ROLE");
bytes32 public constant PAUSER_ROLE = keccak256("PAUSER_ROLE");
bytes32 public constant UPGRADER_ROLE = keccak256("UPGRADER_ROLE");

mapping(bytes32 => bytes32) private roleAdmin;

constructor() {
// Set up role hierarchy
_setRoleAdmin(MINTER_ROLE, DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE);
_setRoleAdmin(PAUSER_ROLE, DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE);
_setRoleAdmin(UPGRADER_ROLE, DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE);

// Grant admin to deployer
_grantRole(DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE, msg.sender);
}

function grantRole(bytes32 role, address account) public {
// Only role admin can grant this role
require(
hasRole(roleAdmin[role], msg.sender),
"Not role admin"
);
_grantRole(role, account);
}

